# Mandatory task initialization
Read `docs/README.md` before every task. Then read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/governance/AI_Agent_Coding_Governance_v2.2.md`, `docs/architecture/Core_Platform_Technical_Specification_V2.2.md`, applicable ADRs and the implementation backlog.

V2.2 is the sole active baseline wherever it conflicts with V2.1.

# Mandatory constraints
- No direct AI provider calls outside the approved AI Gateway.
- Mandatory AI Security Harness and server-side policy revalidation.
- Unknown/C2/C3 classification cannot be sent to external AI.
- Derived data inherits highest parent classification and restrictive ACL.
- RAG ACL is enforced server-side; client-supplied resource IDs are not permissions.
- No cross-service foreign keys or direct cross-service database access.
- Atomic quota reservation, idempotent usage reconciliation and immutable cost ledger.
- Timeouts, bounded retries, idempotency, circuit breakers and policy-approved fallback.
- Fail closed on protected paths when mandatory security/governance dependencies fail.
- No raw sensitive payloads, prompts, OCR text or RAG chunks in telemetry.
- ADR + human approval for architecture/security deviations; independent human review for security changes.
